The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
rstc = devm_reset_control_array_get(&pdev->dev, false, false);
if (IS_ERR(rstc)) {
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
}
```
Reason:
The unconditional printing of the error message when `devm_reset_control_array_get` fails can mislead users into thinking there is a critical error, even when the failure is due to probe deferral (`-EPROBE_DEFER`), which is a normal part of device initialization.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (PTR_ERR(rstc) != -EPROBE_DEFER)
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
```
Reason:
This change adds a conditional check to only print the error message if the error is not due to probe deferral. This prevents misleading error messages during normal device initialization, improving the clarity of the logs.

